# Trained model weights. The code that produces them is versioned; the artefacts are not — they are
# hundreds of megabytes, they are reproducible from a fixed seed, and a repository is a poor
# artefact store. Run `python ml/intent/train.py` to rebuild.
ml/*/model/
ml/*/data/
ml/*/adapters/     # LoRA adapters: 50-200MB of weights, same rule as model/ - never in the repo, never in the bundle

.vercel

# Scraped pages and scratch notes kept in the project root for reference. 700 KB of other
# people's HTML was committed by a `git add -A` that swept the whole working tree; it is not
# source, it is not served (Astro serves src/pages and public only), and it inflates every deploy.
/*.html
/g.mdx
/h.txt
